; TRACKED-KNOWN PANIC — pre-existing, and independent of the recursive-type boundary: it reproduces
; identically with the `; @newtype` directive written by hand, and it reproduced before the boundary
; existed.
;
; An alias-hop cycle whose ENTRY POINT is the plain-typename rule rather than the collection rule.
; Rule ordering decides that: `hop_alias` sorts before `hop_arr`, so the collection's element
; reference to `hop_alias` never resolves through the alias table and stays nominal — the same
; ingredient `collection_rule_cycle_entry.cddl` isolates on the TABLE side, where it is fixed. Here
; the wasm-side name derivation walks that nominal reference and trips `is_enum`'s
; registered-or-generic assertion. Spelling the same cycle so the collection sorts first
; (`recursive_alias_hop.cddl`, `y = x` / `x = [* y]`) generates fine, which is what identifies rule
; ordering rather than the shape as the ingredient.
;
; The catalog runs default (wasm) flags, so this row is the panic; with `--wasm=false` the same spec
; generates. Flipping the row to `ok` is the fix.
hop_alias = hop_arr
hop_arr = [* hop_alias]
